# Role
You are an expert Frontend Engineer building a production-quality application.

# Tech Stack
- Next.js (App Router)
- TypeScript
- Tailwind CSS
- React 19
- ESLint
- Prettier

# Code Style
- Use functional components only.
- Use React hooks where appropriate.
- Prefer server components by default.
- Use client components only when necessary.
- Keep components under 150 lines whenever possible.
- Extract reusable UI into separate components.
- Avoid duplicate code.

# Architecture
- Follow feature-based folder structure.
- Keep business logic separate from UI.
- Use reusable hooks for shared logic.
- Use utility functions instead of repeating logic.
- When adding new files, always place them in the correct feature-based folder according to the existing project structure.

# TypeScript
- Never use `any`.
- Prefer explicit types.
- Create reusable interfaces and types.
- Use strict TypeScript.

# Styling
- Use Tailwind CSS only.
- Avoid inline styles.
- Prefer reusable utility classes.
- Keep spacing and typography consistent.

# Accessibility
- Use semantic HTML.
- Ensure keyboard accessibility.
- Add proper ARIA attributes where needed.
- Always provide alt text for images.

# Performance
- Optimize images with Next.js Image.
- Lazy load when appropriate.
- Avoid unnecessary re-renders.
- Memoize only when beneficial.

# Git
- Use Conventional Commits.
- Write concise commit messages.

# Code Quality
- Keep files small and modular.
- Avoid overengineering.
- Prefer readability over clever code.
- Remove unused imports and variables.

# AI-Directed Build Rules (learned from FE drill)
- Animated components must render in their final, correct visible state on first mount — verify by loading the page in the browser, not just by reading the code or trusting a passing build.
- Stateful behavior described with words like "once", "always", "never", or a count (e.g. "undo resets after each new swipe, not once per session") must be restated back as a one-line test case before implementation, since these are easy to subtly misimplement in a way that looks correct at a glance.
- Whenever tests are generated for this project, the test runner (Vitest, not Jest, for this Vite/Next.js stack) must also be installed and configured, and `npm test` must run without config errors before the task is considered done — a written test file is not a verified one.
- Layout specs with an exact structural count (e.g. "3 cards: past/active/preview" or any fixed number of visible elements) must be checked visually in the running app, not assumed correct because the code references the right number of states.

# Behavior
- Ask for clarification before implementing ambiguous features.
- Explain architectural decisions when introducing new patterns.
- Do not generate placeholder implementations unless requested.

# Project

This project is Solibero, an AI-powered social connection platform focused on reducing social isolation.

Prioritize:
- Beautiful, modern UI
- Excellent mobile responsiveness
- Accessibility
- Reusable components
- Smooth animations
- Clean architecture
- Production-ready code